.next
# `next dev` builds here instead of `.next`, so that a development build and a
# production build cannot overwrite each other (see ROOTLCO_DIST_DIR). It is a
# build directory like any other and must be ignored like one — CI never has it
# because CI never runs `next dev`, so only a developer ever sees the failure
# (P1-26-F-060).
.next-dev
node_modules
coverage

# Playwright run artefacts. Written by the browser smoke, gitignored, and not
# ours to format.
test-results
playwright-report
playwright-report.json

# The web component tier's JSON reporter output (`--outputFile=vitest-web.json`),
# gitignored at .gitignore:85 and equally not ours to format.
#
# Same shape as `.next-dev` above, and CI structurally cannot catch it: the
# web-quality job runs `format:check:web` at _reusable-node-quality.yml:479 and
# only writes this file at :518, so the check always runs BEFORE the artefact
# exists. A developer who runs `npm run test:web-ci` then `format:check:all`
# sees a red gate that hosted CI reports green — which is the worst way round,
# because the local signal is the one being distrusted.
vitest-web.json
